g error in a state that has recently swung Republican could narrow this considerably.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Kim Reynolds (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Iowa's governorship is open with Kim Reynolds retiring, and State Auditor Rob Sand has led Republican Zach Lahn in every recent poll, by margins of five to eleven points. Even Republican-affiliated pollsters show Sand ahead, and averages put the race around six to seven points in his favor. Sand has also vastly outraised Lahn, giving him the resources for a strong closing effort.\n\nThe state's Republican fundamentals keep this from being a lock: Iowa has trended right in recent cycles, and open-seat races can tighten late. Still, prediction markets price Sand's chances near ninety percent, and expert raters broadly call the race a Democratic lean or better. Sand is favored to become the first Iowa Democratic governor in two decades.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8753, "margin": 5.7}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8859, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8669, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8657, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8472, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.8297, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8734, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8592, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.8769, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8877, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8875, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.895, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8938, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.8853, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.8878, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.8885, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9358, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9281, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9084, "margin